     /**
      * Minimum candidate count at which a primitive AI computation can amortize worker dispatch.
      *
-     * <p>The previous value (262144) was appropriate only for a synthetic global batch. Sensors operate on a
-     * per-mob snapshot, so that value effectively disabled the feature on every real server. 256 keeps the
-     * synchronous path for ordinary small scans while allowing dense farms to use the already bounded pool.</p>
+     * <p>9950X measurements show that 128-256 candidates are several times slower when dispatched, while 2048
+     * candidates become profitable with 1024-item partitions. Keeping both floors here prevents configuration from
+     * turning ordinary per-mob scans into a scheduling regression.</p>
      */
